        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nCheck polarity before every label. A passage saying candidate X is the artist, born date, sport, population or symbol asked for is SUPPORT, never counterevidence merely because another passage gives Y. Set support to that passage, fit=direct, observed_slot to the requested role, and counter empty unless there is actual negation or role exclusion. Examples with invented names: two albums both called Evening, one by Mira and one by Noel, support BOTH artists. Two people called Alex born1901 and1873 support BOTH dates. A player practicing golf AND tennis supports BOTH sports. A passage saying London is a birthplace makes London a wrong_argument for a birth-DATE question. Distinguish an asserted false same-role answer from a type error. Before wrong_argument, verify the source actually attributes a DIFFERENT role. Do not invent a disagreement or unknown conflict just to fill the field; differing allowed entities are not contradictions.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is the director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 244, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot (1982 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Escape 2000 and Blood Camp Thatcher) is a 1982 Australian dystopian action film directed by Brian Trenchard-Smith and starring Steve Railsback, Olivia Hussey, Michael Craig, and Lynda Stoner.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 245, \"end\": 346, \"text\": \"The cast is a mix of international actors, Australian soap opera actors and television personalities.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"start\": 347, \"end\": 648, \"text\": \"Widely considered an \\\"Ozploitation\\\" (or Australian exploitation film), the film is notable for its extreme violence and sadistic prison sequences, and it features plot elements of \\\"The Most Dangerous Game\\\", but rather than having human targets hunted for sport by a madman on his own island, the story\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 206, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot (2014 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Elimination Game) is a 2014 Australian dystopian futurist exploitation film directed by Jon Hewitt and co-written by Hewitt and his wife Belinda McClory.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 207, \"end\": 305, \"text\": \"Shot in Australia, the film stars Dominic Purcell, Viva Bianca, Robert Taylor and Belinda McClory.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 306, \"end\": 469, \"text\": \"Inspired by Brian Trenchard-Smith's 1982 \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\", the film features appearances by that film's Carmen Duncan, Roger Ward and the voice of producer Antony I.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 470, \"end\": 521, \"text\": \"Ginnane as television network head Charley Varrick.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 522, \"end\": 611, \"text\": \"In the near future, SEAL Commander Rick Tyler is sent to Libya to assassinate its leader.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"start\": 612, \"end\": 651, \"text\": \"After apparently completing the mission\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 588, \"text\": \"film ) 2 languages Cymraeg فارسی Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia 2014 Australian film Turkey Shoot Australian film poster Directed by Jon Hewitt Written by Belinda McClory Jon Hewitt Based on Turkey Shoot by Antony I.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02\", \"start\": 589, \"end\": 637, \"text\": \"Ginnane Brian Trenchard-Smith Produced by Antony\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 63, \"text\": \"its colour and off-the-wall vitality , was released last year .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 64, \"end\": 167, \"text\": \"Perhaps a remake ( or “ re-invention ” , as director Jon Hewitt called it ) was doomed from the start .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 168, \"end\": 218, \"text\": \"Turkey Shoot is many things ; imitable it is not .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"start\": 219, \"end\": 562, \"text\": \"Explore more on these topics Film Rewatching classic Australian films Australian film reviews Share Reuse this content Comments ( … ) Sign in or create your Guardian account to join the discussion Most viewed Most viewed Film Books Music Art & design TV & radio Stage Classical Games News Opinion Sport Culture Lifestyle Original reporting and\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"director\", \"scope\": \"film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Brian Trenchard-Smith is the director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Brian Trenchard-Smith\", \"quote\": \"Turkey Shoot (1982 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Escape 2000 and Blood Camp Thatcher) is a 1982 Australian dystopian action film directed by Brian Trenchard-Smith and starring Steve Railsback, Olivia Hussey, Michael Craig, and Lynda Stoner.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"director\", \"scope\": \"film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Jon Hewitt is the director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"quote\": \"Turkey Shoot (2014 film) Turkey Shoot (also known as Elimination Game) is a 2014 Australian dystopian futurist exploitation film directed by Jon Hewitt and co-written by Hewitt and his wife Belinda McClory.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"director\", \"scope\": \"film Turkey Shoot\", \"claim\": \"Jon Hewitt is the director of the film Turkey Shoot.\", \"answer\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"quote\": \"film ) 2 languages Cymraeg فارسی Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia 2014 Australian film Turkey Shoot Australian film poster Directed by Jon Hewitt Written by Belinda McClory Jon Hewitt Based on Turkey Shoot by Antony I.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0185-5308b4d1e41d:d03:c0\", \"entity\": \"director\", \"scope\": \"film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\"\", \"claim\": \"Jon Hewitt is the director of the film \\\"Turkey Shoot\\\".\", \"answer\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"quote\": \"Perhaps a remake ( or “ re-invention ” , as director Jon Hewitt called it ) was doomed from the start .\", \"original_document_number\": 4}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Brian Trenchard-Smith\", \"Jon Hewitt\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"Brian Trenchard-Smith\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"Jon Hewitt\", \"